   "source": [
    "# AMA flood susceptibility: full pipeline in Google Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "Runs every stage of the repository in order, keeping data and results in your Google Drive so a disconnected session can pick up where it stopped.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Stage | What it does | Needs |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 0a | Export DEM, NDVI/NDWI, rainfall and LULC layers from Earth Engine | GEE |\n",
    "| 0b | TWI and stream density from the DEM | |\n",
    "| 0c | Align the 12 indicators into one stack (geology and soil from your national maps) | AMA polygon, vector maps |\n",
    "| 1 | Train the U-Net on Sen1Floods11 | **GPU runtime** |\n",
    "| 2a / 2 | Export Sentinel-1 scenes per flood event and map flood polygons | GEE, stage 1 model |\n",
    "| 3 | 1D-CNN susceptibility map | stages 0c and 2 |\n",
    "| 4 | Verify which severe storms became flash floods (Sentinel-1/2 + IMERG) | GEE |\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to use:** edit the *Settings* cell, then run the cells top to bottom. Each stage skips work whose outputs already exist in Drive. For stage 1 choose *Runtime → Change runtime type → GPU*."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "067726de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Settings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "526b05d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ===== edit these =====\n",
    "GEE_PROJECT = "buoyant-facet-392719"",
    "AOI_ASSET   = "projects/buoyant-facet-392719/assets/ama"",     
    "REPO_URL    = "https://github.com/ucflood/flood_vector_py"",   # required
    "WORK        = "/content/drive/MyDrive/ama_flood"",  # persistent folder: repo, data and results\n",
    "\n",
    "# stage 0c: your vector maps in Drive (\"\" if you do not have them yet)\n",
    "AMA_POLYGON = f\"{WORK}/external/AMA.gpkg\"\n",
    "GEOLOGY, GEOLOGY_FIELD = \"\", \"\"                    # e.g. f\"{WORK}/external/geologia.gpkg\", \"FORMACION\"\n",
    "SOIL, SOIL_FIELD       = \"\", \"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "EPOCHS = 100                                       # stage 1, total epochs (re-running continues where it stopped)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a64871b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup: Drive, repository, packages"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ec72ea78",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount(\"/content/drive\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import os, sys, glob, json, shutil, time\n",
    "assert REPO_URL and \"<user>\" not in REPO_URL, \"Set REPO_URL in the Settings cell (your GitHub repo).\"\n",
    "os.makedirs(WORK, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "REPO = f\"{WORK}/ama-flood-susceptibility\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# a folder without .git is a stale copy: move it aside, do not delete it\n",
    "if os.path.isdir(REPO) and not os.path.isdir(f\"{REPO}/.git\"):\n",
    "    old = f\"{REPO}_old_{int(time.time())}\"\n",
    "    shutil.move(REPO, old)\n",
    "    print(\"moved stale folder to\", old)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.isdir(REPO):\n",
    "    !git clone {REPO_URL} \"{REPO}\"\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    !git -C \"{REPO}\" pull\n",
    "\n",
    "assert os.path.exists(f\"{REPO}/requirements-colab.txt\"), (\n",
    "    f\"requirements-colab.txt is not at the root of {REPO}. Found: {sorted(os.listdir(REPO))}. \"\n",
    "    \"Check on GitHub that the repo root has pipeline/, tests/, requirements-colab.txt.\")\n",
    "%cd {REPO}\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, f\"{REPO}/pipeline\")\n",
    "!pip install -q -r requirements-colab.txt\n",
    "!nvidia-smi -L || echo \"No GPU: Runtime > Change runtime type > GPU (needed for stage 1 only)\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "77849e68",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# optional: fast tests of the event, verification and GEE scripts (about 1 minute)\n",
    "!python -m pytest -q tests/test_rain_events.py tests/test_verify_flash.py tests/test_gee_scripts.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cdd80d5b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Earth Engine login\n",
    "A browser window asks you to authorize; the GEE scripts below run with `%run` so they share this session."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "134eb3fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import ee\n",
    "ee.Authenticate()\n",
    "ee.Initialize(project=GEE_PROJECT)\n",
    "os.environ[\"GEE_PROJECT\"] = GEE_PROJECT\n",
    "os.environ[\"AMA_AOI_ASSET\"] = AOI_ASSET\n",
    "if AOI_ASSET:\n",
    "    print(f\"AOI: {ee.FeatureCollection(AOI_ASSET).geometry().area().divide(1e6).getInfo():.0f} km2\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"AOI: placeholder box. Upload the AMA polygon as an asset and set AOI_ASSET.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "076d71b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def collect(drive_folder, dest, names, timeout_min=20):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Copy finished GEE exports from Drive to `dest`. Waits for Drive to sync, and merges\n",
    "    exports that GEE split into tiles (name-0000000000-0000000000.tif).\"\"\"\n",
    "    import rasterio\n",
    "    from rasterio.merge import merge\n",
    "    src = f\"/content/drive/MyDrive/{drive_folder}\"\n",
    "    os.makedirs(dest, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    have = lambda n: os.path.exists(f\"{src}/{n}.tif\") or glob.glob(f\"{src}/{n}-*.tif\")\n",
    "    t0 = time.time()\n",
    "    while [n for n in names if not have(n)]:\n",
    "        missing = [n for n in names if not have(n)]\n",
    "        if time.time() - t0 > timeout_min * 60:\n",
    "            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"not in Drive/{drive_folder} yet: {missing}\")\n",
    "        print(\"waiting for Drive to sync:\", missing)\n",
    "        time.sleep(30)\n",
    "    for n in names:\n",
    "        if os.path.exists(f\"{src}/{n}.tif\"):\n",
    "            shutil.copy(f\"{src}/{n}.tif\", f\"{dest}/{n}.tif\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        tiles = [rasterio.open(t) for t in sorted(glob.glob(f\"{src}/{n}-*.tif\"))]\n",
    "        arr, transform = merge(tiles)\n",
    "        prof = tiles[0].profile; prof.update(height=arr.shape[1], width=arr.shape[2], transform=transform)\n",
    "        with rasterio.open(f\"{dest}/{n}.tif\", \"w\", **prof) as d:\n",
    "            d.write(arr)\n",
    "        for t in tiles: t.close()\n",
    "    print(f\"{len(names)} file(s) -> {dest}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "418e636e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Stage 0a: indicator layers from Earth Engine\n",
    "Sensor, dates and flood windows to exclude are set at the top of `pipeline/00a_gee_export_layers.py`. The cell waits until the exports finish (minutes to tens of minutes)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cc4d3ce8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "LAYERS = \"data/interim/layers\"\n",
    "L0A = [\"elevation\", \"slope\", \"aspect\", \"relief_amplitude\", \"ndvi\", \"ndwi\", \"rainfall\", \"lulc\"]\n",
    "if all(os.path.exists(f\"{LAYERS}/{n}.tif\") for n in L0A):\n",
    "    print(\"stage 0a already done\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    os.environ[\"GEE_DRIVE_FOLDER\"] = \"AMA_layers\"\n",
    "    os.environ[\"GEE_WAIT\"] = \"1\"\n",
    "    %run pipeline/00a_gee_export_layers.py\n",
    "    collect(\"AMA_layers\", LAYERS, L0A)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "574bd6d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Stage 0b: TWI and stream density"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3f8904f6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if os.path.exists(f\"{LAYERS}/twi.tif\") and os.path.exists(f\"{LAYERS}/stream_density.tif\"):\n",
    "    print(\"stage 0b already done\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    !python pipeline/00b_terrain_hydrology.py --dem {LAYERS}/elevation.tif --out-dir {LAYERS}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e339bc2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Stage 0c: 12-layer stack\n",
    "Upload `AMA.gpkg` (and the geology / soil maps) to `WORK/external` first. Without a soil map you can set `SOIL_OPENLANDMAP = True` in 00a and copy `soil_openlandmap.tif` as `soil.tif`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "217c46a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "STACK = \"data/processed/stack\"\n",
    "args = f'--layers-dir {LAYERS} --aoi \"{AMA_POLYGON}\" --out-dir {STACK}'\n",
    "if GEOLOGY: args += f' --geology \"{GEOLOGY}\" --geology-field {GEOLOGY_FIELD}'\n",
    "if SOIL:    args += f' --soil \"{SOIL}\" --soil-field {SOIL_FIELD}'\n",
    "!python pipeline/00c_build_stack.py {args}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "05ab3685",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Stage 1: train the U-Net on Sen1Floods11 (GPU)\n",
    "The chips go to the local disk (fast) and are downloaded again in each new session; checkpoints and `history.csv` go to Drive. If Colab disconnects, run the cells again: training continues from the last epoch."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3ada1e8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import auth\n",
    "auth.authenticate_user()                      # gsutil access to the public Sen1Floods11 bucket\n",
    "S1F = \"/content/sen1floods11\"\n",
    "if not os.path.isdir(f\"{S1F}/files/S1\"):\n",
    "    !mkdir -p {S1F}/files/S1 {S1F}/files/Labels\n",
    "    !gsutil -q cp gs://sen1floods11/v1.1/splits/flood_handlabeled/flood_train_data.csv gs://sen1floods11/v1.1/splits/flood_handlabeled/flood_valid_data.csv gs://sen1floods11/v1.1/splits/flood_handlabeled/flood_test_data.csv {S1F}/\n",
    "    !gsutil -m -q rsync -r gs://sen1floods11/v1.1/data/flood_events/HandLabeled/S1Hand {S1F}/files/S1\n",
    "    !gsutil -m -q rsync -r gs://sen1floods11/v1.1/data/flood_events/HandLabeled/LabelHand {S1F}/files/Labels\n",
    "print(len(os.listdir(f\"{S1F}/files/S1\")), \"S1 chips\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a58b4b6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CKPT = \"results/checkpoints\"\n",
    "!python pipeline/01_train_sen1floods11.py --train-csv {S1F}/flood_train_data.csv --valid-csv {S1F}/flood_valid_data.csv --test-csv {S1F}/flood_test_data.csv --s1-dir {S1F}/files/S1 --lbl-dir {S1F}/files/Labels --out-dir {CKPT} --epochs {EPOCHS} --resume"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2bc9e9e0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "h = pd.read_csv(f\"{CKPT}/history.csv\")\n",
    "ax = h.plot(x=\"epoch\", y=[\"flood_iou\", \"val_flood_iou\"], figsize=(7, 3), title=\"Flood IoU\")\n",
    "print(h.tail(3).to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dc12cf1b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Stage 2a: Sentinel-1 scenes per flood event\n",
    "One post-flood scene and one low-water reference per event, **same orbit pass**. Pick the dates from the Asunción river gauge (see `data/events/ama_events_filtered.csv`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "67a13e33",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "S1_SCENES = {                                  # name: [start, end, orbit pass]  (placeholders: edit)\n",
    "    \"2019_05_post\": [\"2019-05-20\", \"2019-05-31\", \"DESCENDING\"],\n",
    "    \"2019_05_pre\":  [\"2019-01-01\", \"2019-01-31\", \"DESCENDING\"],\n",
    "}\n",
    "EVENTS = {\"2019_05\": (\"2019_05_post\", \"2019_05_pre\")}    # event: (post scene, reference scene)\n",
    "\n",
    "S1DIR = \"data/interim/s1\"\n",
    "names = [f\"S1_{k}\" for k in S1_SCENES] + [\"GSW_occurrence\"]\n",
    "if all(os.path.exists(f\"{S1DIR}/{n}.tif\") for n in names):\n",
    "    print(\"stage 2a already done\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    os.environ[\"S1_SCENES\"] = json.dumps(S1_SCENES)\n",
    "    os.environ[\"GEE_DRIVE_FOLDER\"] = \"AMA_S1\"\n",
    "    os.environ[\"GEE_WAIT\"] = \"1\"\n",
    "    %run pipeline/02a_gee_export_s1.py\n",
    "    collect(\"AMA_S1\", S1DIR, names)"
   ]
  },
